// For a language that indexes strings by rune, not being able to write a rune
// by codepoint was a conspicuous gap. The value is a codepoint, not a byte,
// even for \xNN — a raw high byte would build a string the rest of the language
// cannot read.
println("\x41\x42")
println("é")
println("\u{e9}")
println("\u{1F600}")
println(String.count("\u{1F600}"))
println("\u{1F600}" == "😀")
